sc: an external 3D range reads every sheet it spans

Calc did not evaluate a range over several sheets of another file.
Typed before the file was cached, 'file:///…/[source.fods]S1:S3'!A1
lost its last sheet at once and read S1 alone: the parser takes the
span from the cache only. Typed after, convertToTokenArray gave up on
purpose and the range read as empty, so SUM was 0. The parser's try
as a single reference also left the raw path as a second file ID; an
update named that phantom link as failed while the real one changed
the values. Saved to XLSX the range came back as text: Calc wrote
'[1]S1':'S3'!A1:A1, which its own import cannot parse, and no cached
cells. Patch 0131's check could not see the sheets past the first,
so an update kept no saved value when they were gone (Ely R20.33).

- The parser reads the sheet names of a file it knows none of before
  the span, as a single reference already loads the file. The
  single-reference try clears the file name it gives up on, so no
  phantom ID is made.
- A last sheet the file lacks makes no range: a compiled reference
  with a deleted sheet answers #REF! instead of reading the first.
  INDIRECT names both ends of such a span as looked up and answers
  Err:540 while links await the user's check, #REF! after.
- getDoubleRefTokensFromSrcDoc names each sheet (it named the second
  for all), and convertToTokenArray gives a matrix per sheet, blank
  ones empty, as the cache and the XLSX export expect.
- SUM, SUMSQ, PRODUCT, AVERAGE, COUNT and COUNTA (IterateParameters)
  read every matrix. A function that takes one matrix answers
  Err:502 for several, as upstream did before.
- Excel A1 writes the span as Excel does, 'dir/[file]S1:S3'!A1, and
  OOXML as '[N]S1:S3'!A1; both parse again.
- A 3D lookup records every sheet it spans, blank ones too, so when
  one is gone the update fails, names the file and keeps the values.
- An update places each compiled span by its two named ends in the
  new file, the start swapped when they swapped, and gives the cache
  the file's new sheet list, so an inserted or moved sheet counts.

